## guest_and_provisional_account_containment

### Current Progress
- **Phase 1: Access and safeguard audit** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 2: Critical containment** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 3: Trust policy and capability registry** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 4: HTTP and WebSocket enforcement** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 5: Tiered distributed limiting** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 6: Onboarding and observability** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 7: Adversarial rollout verification** - ✅ Complete

### Next Steps
- [x] Guest/provisional writes now default-deny before handlers; the reviewed
  public exceptions are auth/recovery, bounded public page views, public-page
  datasource rendering without client/stored env disclosure, route-owner-enabled
  voice tokens, legacy guest order lookup, and global chat.
- [x] Guest checkout and wallet credit creation are unavailable. The unsafe full
  page list and individual visitor APIs are removed; public user reads use a
  dedicated profile DTO.
- [x] `AccountTrustPolicy` uses persisted account creation time, current TOTP
  state and server UTC. It returns `account_provisional` with unlock metadata;
  lookup failure denies mutations.
- [x] Redis budgets cover tenant/IP/account mutation classes, auth, WebSocket
  upgrades and reconnect-resistant tiered chat. Redis failure denies mutations
  and chat without taking browse reads offline.
- [x] The responsive dismissible notice explains browsing/chat availability,
  optional TOTP immediate unlock and the server countdown. Aggregate safeguard
  telemetry is admin-only and content-free.
- [x] Verification passed on 2026-08-20: complete backend suite; WS/security race
  suite; all 213 frontend tests; Biome lint; TypeScript; native-dialog policy;
  production build; todo/reference/diff checks. Browser automation was not
  available, so countdown, stale-tab and reconnect behavior are covered by
  deterministic policy, middleware, WS and component tests.

### Audit Record
- 2026-08-20: confirmed that registration issues normal tokens and the default
  `member` role immediately; neither account age, email verification, nor TOTP
  gates ordinary authenticated mutations.
- 2026-08-20: confirmed unauthenticated individual media-history tombstoning and
  broader guest media controls, unauthenticated Grengo control-plane forwarding,
  unrestricted authenticated wallet credit, public private-page listing,
  spoofable WebSocket display identity, permissionless authenticated teleport,
  globally broadcast infrastructure telemetry, unrestricted visitor IP/identity
  analytics, and reconnect-local chat/media limiting gaps.
- 2026-08-20: existing safeguards and intentional exceptions were traced across
  routes, services, repositories, middleware, migrations, specs, and tests. No
  application code or production state was changed during this planning audit.

